WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.192
The school Week Seven reading includes endocrine physiology, diabetes medicines and endocrine emergencies. This workshop turns those topics into an assessment and treatment-response sequence.
学校第7周阅读包括内分泌生理、糖尿病药及内分泌急症。本课把它们转换成评估及治疗反应顺序。

00:00:12.192 --> 00:00:23.904
Measure glucose early in altered function, seizures, stroke-like symptoms and relevant acute illness. A known diabetes diagnosis is not required to have a dangerous glucose problem.
功能变、抽搐、中风样症状及相关急病时，应早测糖；发生危险血糖问题不必先有糖尿病诊断。

00:00:23.904 --> 00:00:36.528
Correct confirmed low glucose promptly through the safe route while supporting ABCs. A glucose result must not delay treatment of inadequate ventilation or another visible life threat.
确认低糖后应及时经安全途径纠正，同时支持ABC；血糖结果不能延误通气不足或其他可见生命威胁处理。

00:00:36.528 --> 00:00:47.712
Then ask why it happened and whether the patient truly recovered. Persistent abnormalities can reflect recurrence, a second disease or a different primary diagnosis.
随后问为何发生、是否真正恢复；持续异常可来自复发、第二疾病或不同首要诊断。

00:00:47.712 --> 00:01:01.440
Endocrine cells release hormones into surrounding fluid and the circulation. Exocrine glands use ducts for substances such as digestive enzymes or sweat; their role is not simply waste elimination.
内分泌细胞把激素释放到周围液及循环，外分泌腺经导管输送消化酶或汗等物，其作用并非只是排废。

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:12.672
A circulating hormone affects cells with the relevant receptors and response machinery. More hormone is not always equivalent to a normal response if the target is resistant.
循环激素作用于有相应受体及反应机制的细胞；靶细胞抵抗时，激素多不一定等于正常反应。

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:25.248
Receptor stimulation can change membrane signaling, enzyme activity or gene expression. Catecholamine effects can be rapid, while many steroid-mediated effects develop more slowly.
受体刺激可改膜信号、酶活动或基因表达；儿茶酚胺可很快起效，许多类固醇效应发展较慢。

00:01:25.248 --> 00:01:36.912
Endocrine emergencies can result from deficient secretion, excess secretion, resistance or disrupted feedback. Relate the mechanism to the actual physiological problem.
内分泌急症可来自分泌不足、过量、抵抗或反馈失调，需把机制连到真实生理问题。

00:01:36.912 --> 00:01:47.640
Negative feedback means that the response tends to reduce the original disturbance. For example, rising glucose stimulates insulin-related effects that lower glucose.
负反馈指反应倾向于减少原始偏离，例如糖升高会刺激胰岛素相关效应，使糖降低。

00:01:47.640 --> 00:02:00.312
Thyroid signaling uses an axis: hypothalamic releasing hormone, pituitary TSH and thyroid hormone. Thyroid hormone feeds back to reduce excessive upstream drive.
甲状腺信号使用轴：下丘脑释放激素、垂体TSH及甲状腺激素；甲状腺激素反馈减少上游过强驱动。

00:02:00.312 --> 00:02:11.064
The level of failure matters. A peripheral gland problem and a pituitary control problem can produce different laboratory patterns despite similar target-hormone deficiency.
故障层次很重要，外周腺体与垂体控制问题，可在类似靶激素缺乏时呈现不同化验模式。

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:22.032
The field task is usually recognition and support rather than a full hormone-level diagnosis. Ask about established disease, replacement treatment and current stressors.
现场任务通常是识别支持，而不是完整激素化验诊断；需问已知疾病、替代治疗及当前应激。

00:02:22.032 --> 00:02:34.416
The anterior pituitary produces hormones including TSH, ACTH, growth hormone, prolactin, FSH and LH. Not all six are gonadotropins.
垂体前叶产生TSH、ACTH、生长激素、催乳素、FSH及LH等；六种并非全是促性腺激素。

00:02:34.416 --> 00:02:45.096
The posterior pituitary stores and releases ADH and oxytocin made by hypothalamic neurons. Production and release locations are therefore different.
垂体后叶储存释放由下丘脑神经元产生的ADH及催产素，因此产生及释放位置不同。

00:02:45.096 --> 00:02:57.000
ACTH stimulates the adrenal cortex to support cortisol production. The medulla releases catecholamines through sympathetic neural stimulation, not the same ACTH route.
ACTH刺激肾上腺皮质支持皮质醇产生；髓质经交感神经刺激释放儿茶酚胺，并不是同一ACTH路径。

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:07.368
These distinctions explain why control failure, replacement medicines and stress can alter glucose, vascular responses and water balance in different ways.
这些区别解释控制失败、替代药及应激，为何会以不同方式改变血糖、血管反应及水分平衡。

00:03:07.368 --> 00:03:20.400
Insulin supports glucose use and storage and restrains hepatic glucose production, fat breakdown and ketone generation. It has ongoing basal roles, not simply an on-off switch after meals.
胰岛素支持糖利用储存，并抑肝产糖、脂肪分解及生酮；它有持续基础功能，不只是餐后开关。

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:31.416
Not every cell needs insulin for glucose entry. The brain and red cells use largely insulin-independent entry, so the book all-cells-need-insulin statement is too broad.
不是所有细胞进糖都需胰岛素；脑及红细胞主要使用不依赖胰岛素的进入，因此书中“所有细胞都需”的句子过宽。

00:03:31.416 --> 00:03:44.016
Glucagon helps the liver make glucose available, while stress hormones can raise production and reduce effective insulin action. Infection or another acute illness can therefore destabilize control.
胰高血糖素帮助肝提供可用糖，应激激素又可增产糖并减有效胰岛素作用，因此感染等急病可使控制失稳。

00:03:44.016 --> 00:03:54.960
The brain still needs a reliable energy supply, so severe low glucose is urgent. Avoid replacing this principle with an exact universal time-to-injury countdown.
脑仍需可靠能量供应，因此严重低糖紧急，但不能把这个原则改成适用于所有人的精确损伤倒计时。

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:08.424
Diabetes mellitus is a group of disorders of glucose regulation, not one uniform illness. Insulin deficiency, resistance and progressive secretion problems contribute in different combinations.
糖尿病是一组血糖调节障碍，不是统一一种病；胰岛素不足、抵抗及逐渐分泌问题，可按不同组合参与。

00:04:08.424 --> 00:04:19.344
Long-term disease can injure vessels, nerves, retina and kidneys. Neuropathy and cardiovascular disease can alter how an acute illness presents.
长期疾病可损血管、神经、视网膜及肾，神经病及心血管病又可改变急病表现。

00:04:19.344 --> 00:04:30.552
Ask about the actual treatment, usual glucose pattern, recent illness and access to food or medicines. An insulin user is not automatically a type-one patient.
需问真实治疗、平常糖模式、近期病及食物药物获取；使用胰岛素不自动等于一型。

00:04:30.552 --> 00:04:42.360
Diabetes can coexist with stroke, sepsis, trauma or poisoning. The diagnosis should trigger useful checks rather than explain every new symptom by itself.
糖尿病可与中风、脓毒症、创伤或中毒并存，诊断应触发有用核查，不能独自解释全部新症状。

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:50.784
Type one commonly involves autoimmune beta-cell loss and essential insulin replacement. It can begin in adults as well as children.
一型常涉及自身免疫性β细胞丢失，必须胰岛素替代，但可在成人或儿童起病。

00:04:50.784 --> 00:04:59.880
Type two involves resistance and variable impairment of secretion. Some patients use insulin, and type-two patients can develop DKA.
二型涉及抵抗及不同程度分泌受损；部分使用胰岛素，而且二型也可发生DKA。

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:11.136
Gestational diabetes relates to pregnancy physiology and needs the actual pregnancy-specific plan. A general adult rule is not automatically an obstetric instruction.
妊娠糖尿病与孕期生理相关，需要真实妊娠特定计划；一般成人规则不自动变成产科指令。

00:05:11.136 --> 00:05:22.944
Do not diagnose type from age, body size or a drug name alone. DKA and HHS have typical associations, but overlaps and first presentations are possible.
不能只靠年龄、体型或药名诊断分型；DKA与HHS虽有典型关联，但可能重叠或首次就以急症呈现。

00:05:22.944 --> 00:05:33.720
Low glucose can follow excess insulin effect, insulin-secretagogue medicines, reduced intake, activity, alcohol, renal disease or acute illness.
低糖可在胰岛素效应过多、促分泌药、摄入少、活动、酒精、肾病或急病后发生。

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:48.072
Autonomic warning symptoms may include sweating, tremor, hunger and palpitations. Brain dysfunction can cause confusion, poor coordination, altered speech, seizures or reduced responsiveness.
自主神经警告可有汗、颤抖、饥饿、心悸；脑功能受损可混乱、协调差、言语变、抽搐或反应下降。

00:05:48.072 --> 00:05:57.696
Some people have reduced warning awareness or a modified pulse response. Absence of sweating or tachycardia does not exclude low glucose.
部分患者警告觉察减少，或脉反应被改变；无汗或无心动过速不能排低糖。

00:05:57.696 --> 00:06:08.208
The locally checked treatment gate is below four millimoles per liter. Interpret a reliable measurement with symptoms and treat promptly through an airway-safe route.
当地核对的处理门槛为低于4毫摩尔每升；需结合症状解释可靠测量，并经气道安全途径及时治。

00:06:08.208 --> 00:06:20.304
Low glucose can look like stroke, intoxication or a behavioural crisis. Check it in a relevant altered presentation rather than relying on appearance or a substance history.
低糖可像中风、中毒或行为危机；相关意识功能异常时应测，不能只靠外观或物质史。

00:06:20.304 --> 00:06:31.272
There is no age-fifty-five minimum or requirement for a known diabetes history. A young or previously undiagnosed patient can have a severe glucose emergency.
不存在55岁最低年龄，也不必有已知糖尿病史；年轻或从未确诊者都可能严重血糖急症。

00:06:31.272 --> 00:06:44.472
After correction, repeat speech, limb function, face, awareness and the full primary assessment as indicated. Preserve last-known-well information when a stroke remains possible.
纠正后需按指征重查语言、肢体、面部、意识及完整初步评估；仍可能中风时需保留最后正常时刻。

00:06:44.472 --> 00:06:54.864
A better glucose or partial improvement does not exclude a second condition. Do not withhold urgent stroke evaluation merely because the first number was low.
糖变好或部分改善，不能排第二疾病；不能只因首次数字低就停止紧急中风评估。

00:06:54.864 --> 00:07:06.408
Use the actual approved meter and sampling process, recording the value in millimoles per liter with time. A device reading HI or LO is not an exact number you should invent.
应使用真实获准仪器及采样流程，记毫摩尔每升数值及时间。仪器HI或LO不代表可以编一个精确数字。

00:07:06.408 --> 00:07:18.576
Poor perfusion, sample contamination or technical error can affect a capillary measurement. Follow the device checks and repeat or obtain an appropriate alternative when the result does not fit.
灌注差、样本污染或技术错误可影响毛细血管测量；结果不符时，应依器械核查并复测或取得适当替代。

00:07:18.576 --> 00:07:31.680
A continuous glucose sensor measures interstitial information and may not exactly match rapidly changing blood glucose. Assess the patient and use the actual confirmation process when needed.
持续血糖感测器测间质信息，未必精确对应快速变化的血糖；需评患者，并在必要时使用真实确认流程。

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:46.248
If testing is unavailable or uncertainty persists in a critical patient, obtain clinical support while providing the safe indicated care. Do not give every unexplained coma an automatic glucose-naloxone cocktail.
危急患者检测不可得或持续不确定时，应在安全有指征照护同时求临床支持；不能每个未知昏迷都自动给糖加纳洛酮套餐。

00:07:46.248 --> 00:07:55.824
For an appropriate conscious patient who follows commands and can swallow without aspiration or choking risk, oral glucose is the preferred simple route.
适当清醒、能遵指令且可安全吞咽、无误吸窒息风险者，口服葡萄糖是优先简单途径。

00:07:55.824 --> 00:08:06.696
The checked local monograph gives fifteen grams of glucose, or a labelled tablet equivalent. The amount of glucose is different from the total mass of a tube or pouch.
核对当地专论给15克葡萄糖，或标示片剂等量；葡萄糖量不同于整支或整袋总质量。

00:08:06.696 --> 00:08:18.600
The local repeat line is five minutes as required, with ongoing assessment and repeat glucose. Do not put gel, a drink or loose gauze into an unprotected airway.
当地重复行为按需五分钟，并需持续评估复测糖；不能把胶、饮料或松纱布塞进未受保护气道。

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:31.392
Once recovery and safe intake allow, longer-acting carbohydrate can sustain correction through the actual plan. Food does not replace investigation of recurrent or unexplained hypoglycemia.
恢复并可安全摄入后，可依真实计划用较长效碳水维持纠正；食物不能代替反复或不明低糖的调查。

00:08:31.392 --> 00:08:43.752
For indicated adult PCP intravenous correction, the currently checked pathway uses ten to twenty-five grams of dextrose, equivalent to one hundred to two hundred fifty milliliters of D ten.
有指征成人PCP静脉纠正时，当前核对路径使用10至25克葡萄糖，等于D10的100至250毫升。

00:08:43.752 --> 00:08:56.232
Verify the bag and prescribed amount, assess a patent line and monitor it throughout delivery. A previous flashback alone is not a permanent guarantee that the infusion remains intravascular.
需核袋和规定量，评通畅管，并在给入期间持续查；以前见回血不能永久保证仍在血管内。

00:08:56.232 --> 00:09:08.424
Dextrose extravasation can injure tissue. Stop delivery and follow the actual extravasation process with clinical help if pain, swelling, leakage or another concern appears.
葡萄糖外渗可伤组织；有痛、肿、漏或其他担忧时，应停止给入，依真实外渗流程及临床援助处理。

00:09:08.424 --> 00:09:22.344
The older Nancy D fifty recipe is not silently substituted for current D ten. The monograph pediatric PCP line specifically says older than twelve; do not scale the adult routine to younger children.
不能把旧Nancy D50配方悄悄替代当前D10；专论儿童PCP行明确为大于12岁，不能把成人常规缩放给更小儿童。

00:09:22.344 --> 00:09:32.376
D ten contains ten grams per hundred milliliters, or point one gram per milliliter. Ten grams therefore corresponds to one hundred milliliters.
D10每100毫升含10克，即每毫升0.1克，因此10克对应100毫升。

00:09:32.376 --> 00:09:42.264
Twenty-five grams corresponds to two hundred fifty milliliters of that verified concentration. These volumes change if the product concentration changes.
25克对应该已核浓度的250毫升；产品浓度改变，体积就改变。

00:09:42.264 --> 00:09:56.424
For comparison, D fifty contains point five grams per milliliter, so its volume cannot be copied onto a D ten bag. Confusing grams, milligrams and milliliters creates a large error.
比较之下，D50每毫升0.5克，因此它的体积不能复制到D10袋。混淆克、毫克及毫升，会造成大错误。

00:09:56.424 --> 00:10:09.432
Read back the drug, prescribed grams, concentration, calculated volume and route, then reassess. A correct calculation does not replace the indication or a reliable line.
需回读药名、规定克数、浓度、计算体积及途径，再复评；算对不能代替指征及可靠通路。

00:10:09.432 --> 00:10:21.120
The current local monograph uses a sealed three-milligram intranasal kit when confirmed low glucose cannot be safely treated orally and IV access is unavailable.
当前当地专论使用密封3毫克鼻用套件，用于确认低糖、不能安全口服且静脉不可得。

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:33.360
The source excludes intranasal use under four years. A second dose at fifteen minutes if needed requires prior CliniCall consultation, with a maximum of six milligrams.
该来源排除四岁以下鼻用；必要时15分钟第二剂需先CliniCall咨询，最大6毫克。

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:46.392
This is distinct from the older one-milligram IM textbook or exam reference. Verify the actual kit and instructions; the patient does not need to inhale deliberately for nasal administration.
这与旧教材或考试参考的1毫克肌注不同；应核真实套件说明，鼻用不需要患者主动吸气。

00:10:46.392 --> 00:10:59.640
Glucagon depends on available liver glycogen and can cause vomiting. Continue airway support, glucose reassessment and escalation while it acts; do not wait passively for fifteen minutes.
胰高血糖素依赖可用肝糖原，并可引呕吐；起效期间需继续气道支持、复糖及升级，不能被动等15分钟。

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:09.672
Recheck glucose after treatment and compare the actual function. A better number without recovery needs another explanation and continued support.
治疗后应复测糖并比较真实功能；数值变好但未恢复，需另找解释并持续支持。

00:11:09.672 --> 00:11:23.784
Ask about insulin and oral medicines, intake, activity, alcohol, kidney function and acute illness. A low-glucose episode can reveal infection or a medicine problem rather than merely a missed snack.
需问胰岛素和口服药、摄入活动、酒精、肾功能及急病；一次低糖可能揭示感染或药问题，不只是少吃点心。

00:11:23.784 --> 00:11:35.040
Insulin or secretagogue action can outlast the initial rescue glucose, so recurrence is possible. Renal impairment and poor intake can increase the difficulty.
胰岛素或促分泌作用可比最初救援糖持续更久，因此可能复发；肾受损及摄入差会增加难度。

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:47.304
Document timing, route, amount and response, then arrange the appropriate care plan. One normal recheck does not automatically justify leaving a high-risk patient.
应记录时刻、途径、量和反应，再安排适当计划；一次复糖正常不自动支持留下高危患者。

00:11:47.304 --> 00:12:00.048
The local adult nonconveyance criteria require an explained fully resolved episode, normal mentation and observations, glucose at least four and no fever or concurrent acute illness.
当地成人不转运条件要求原因可解释、完全缓解、精神观察正常、糖至少4，且无热或同时急病。

00:12:00.048 --> 00:12:13.872
The page excludes overdose, excessive alcohol, oral hypoglycemic medicines and another treated hypoglycemic episode within twenty-four hours. Do not replace that list with personal reassurance.
该页排除过量、酒精过多、口服降糖药，以及24小时内另一次需治低糖；不能用个人安慰替代这些条件。

00:12:13.872 --> 00:12:25.248
It also requires a responsible adult for at least four hours and the follow-up and documentation process. These conditions are necessary checks, not a universal discharge order.
还需至少四小时有责任成人陪伴，以及后续和文件流程；这些是必要核查，不是通用离院医嘱。

00:12:25.248 --> 00:12:39.000
Use the actual capacity, informed-refusal and consultation pathway, especially when any criterion is uncertain. A signature or a glucose of four alone cannot establish a safe decision.
任何条件不清时，尤其需用真实决定能力、知情拒绝及咨询路径；单个签名或糖为4，不能证明决定安全。

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:49.488
A forty-two-year-old using insulin has been unusually active and eaten little. Now there is sweating, confusion and slurred speech, with glucose two point four.
一位42岁胰岛素使用者，活动特别多且进食少，现在出汗、混乱、言语含糊，糖2.4。

00:12:49.488 --> 00:13:02.040
Support current ABCs while a partner establishes last known well and checks focal findings. The likely low-glucose mechanism does not remove the need to assess stroke and other causes.
应支持当前ABC，同时由搭档建立最后正常及查局灶；很可能低糖，并不取消中风及其他病因评估。

00:13:02.040 --> 00:13:13.128
Determine whether the patient can follow commands and swallow safely. Use oral treatment only if those conditions hold; otherwise use the actual authorized nonoral pathway.
要判断能否遵指令及安全吞咽；仅条件成立时口服，否则使用真实获准非口服路径。

00:13:13.128 --> 00:13:22.704
Recheck glucose, speech, face, limbs, awareness and breathing after treatment. Keep the timeline and all residual findings for the receiving plan.
治疗后需复糖、语言、面部、肢体、意识及呼吸，并为接收计划保留时间线及全部残余表现。

00:13:22.704 --> 00:13:34.752
In a separate original case, a fifty-three-year-old taking gliclazide has eaten little during kidney illness. Initial treatment raises glucose to six point five and improves function.
另一原创病例中，53岁格列齐特使用者在肾病急变期间进食少；初治糖升6.5且功能改善。

00:13:34.752 --> 00:13:46.296
Later glucose falls to three point one and confusion recurs. The medicine and illness may outlast the initial rescue, so the first improvement was not the end of the problem.
之后糖降3.1并再次混乱；药与疾病可能比最初救援持续更久，因此首次改善不是问题结束。

00:13:46.296 --> 00:13:58.320
Repeat the appropriate airway-safe treatment and assessment, seek clinical support and arrange hospital evaluation. Do not treat this as an uncomplicated resolved adult episode.
需重复适当气道安全处理及评估、求临床支持并安排医院评估，不能当作简单已缓解成人发作。

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:10.392
Persistent focal findings after glucose correction also require urgent stroke evaluation rather than repeated treatment for a now-normal number. Match the action to the actual ongoing threat.
纠糖后仍有局灶表现，也需紧急中风评估，而不是反复治疗现已正常数字；行动应匹配真实持续威胁。

00:14:10.392 --> 00:14:22.104
When filtered glucose exceeds the kidney reabsorptive capacity, glucose remains in tubular fluid. Water follows the osmotic effect and urine losses can increase.
滤过糖超过肾重吸收能力时，糖留在小管液内；渗透作用带水，尿丢失可增加。

00:14:22.104 --> 00:14:32.976
The patient can lose water and electrolytes despite drinking because thirst may not keep up. Vomiting, illness or reduced access to fluids can compound the deficit.
即使喝水，也可能因口渴饮量赶不上而丢水电解质；呕吐、疾病或无法获得水可加缺失。

00:14:32.976 --> 00:14:44.568
Hypertonic extracellular fluid also draws water from cells. This helps explain both whole-body depletion and neurological dysfunction in severe hyperglycemic states.
高张细胞外液还从细胞内吸水，有助解释严重高糖状态的全身不足及神经功能异常。

00:14:44.568 --> 00:14:55.464
Early frequent urination can become reduced output as perfusion or kidney function worsens. Do not require ongoing polyuria to recognize a late sick patient.
早期频尿可在灌注或肾恶化后转尿少，因此识别晚期重病不必强求持续多尿。

00:14:55.464 --> 00:15:07.320
In DKA, insufficient effective insulin and counter-regulatory hormones promote hepatic glucose production and fat breakdown. Ketone production can exceed safe handling.
DKA中，有效胰岛素不足及反调节激素促进肝产糖和脂肪分解，酮生成可超安全处理能力。

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:22.464
Ketone-associated acids contribute to metabolic acidosis, while glucose-related diuresis and vomiting cause fluid and electrolyte loss. These processes interact but are not measured completely by one glucose.
酮相关酸参与代谢酸中毒，糖相关利尿和呕吐则丢液电解质；它们互相作用，但单个糖值不能完整测量。

00:15:22.464 --> 00:15:35.352
Possible findings include thirst, vomiting, abdominal pain, dehydration, deep breathing and altered awareness. Neither fruity breath nor every classic symptom is required.
可能表现有口渴、吐、腹痛、脱水、深呼吸及意识变；不必有水果气味或全部典型症状。

00:15:35.352 --> 00:15:47.832
DKA can occur with type two or a first diabetes presentation and can coexist with infection, stroke or MI. Ordinary hyperglycemia does not inevitably progress to DKA.
DKA可在二型或首次糖尿病呈现，并可与感染、中风或MI并存；普通高糖并非必然进展DKA。

00:15:47.832 --> 00:15:59.280
Kussmaul-type deep breathing can be a respiratory response to metabolic acidosis. Greater effective ventilation removes carbon dioxide and helps defend pH.
Kussmaul样深呼吸可为代谢酸中毒的呼吸反应；有效通气增加排出CO2，帮助维持pH。

00:15:59.280 --> 00:16:09.312
Do not label this harmless anxiety or ask the patient to rebreathe into a paper bag. That could increase carbon dioxide and worsen the acid-base problem.
不能称为无害焦虑，也不能让纸袋重呼吸，否则可能增CO2并加重酸碱问题。

00:16:09.312 --> 00:16:24.168
Fatigue, declining awareness or airway failure still requires support. If advanced airway intervention becomes necessary, the team must plan to preserve needed ventilation rather than automatically impose a low fixed rate.
疲劳、意识下降或气道失败仍需支持；若必须高级气道，团队需计划保留所需通气，不能自动套低固定频率。

00:16:24.168 --> 00:16:39.720
At PCP level, identify deterioration, provide effective basic assistance and obtain appropriate advanced help. Deep breathing does not by itself authorize intubation or an arbitrary very rapid bagging rate.
PCP需识别恶化、有效基础辅助并求适当高级援助；深呼吸本身不授权插管或任意极快挤囊。

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:51.144
Osmotic urine loss and vomiting can deplete total-body potassium. At the same time, altered distribution can leave the measured blood potassium normal or elevated.
渗透性尿丢失和呕吐可耗总体钾，同时分布改变可使实测血钾正常或偏高。

00:16:51.144 --> 00:16:59.160
These are different compartments. A high blood concentration therefore does not prove that the body has an adequate total store.
这是不同区室，因此血浓度高不证明全身总储量足够。

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:10.296
Insulin therapy can shift potassium into cells and lower the blood value. Definitive therapy needs appropriate electrolyte measurements, monitoring and adjustment.
胰岛素治疗可把钾移入细胞并降血值，因此确定治疗需要适当电解质测量、监测及调整。

00:17:10.296 --> 00:17:22.008
Monitor relevant rhythm changes and request help for instability. Do not give insulin, potassium or bicarbonate from a textbook algorithm without the actual advanced authority and plan.
需监相关节律变化，不稳时求援；不能没有真实高级权限计划，就照教材算法给胰岛素、钾或碳酸氢钠。

00:17:22.008 --> 00:17:35.448
HHS often develops in type-two diabetes with another illness and inadequate fluid intake. Severe hyperglycemia and osmotic losses can produce major depletion and hyperosmolality.
HHS常在二型伴另一急病及液体摄入不足发展，严重高糖及渗透丢失可形成显著不足和高渗。

00:17:35.448 --> 00:17:47.712
Some effective insulin may limit extensive ketogenesis while failing to control glucose adequately. Significant DKA-like acidosis is less typical, but mixed states occur.
部分有效胰岛素可能限制大量生酮，却不足控制糖；明显DKA样酸中毒较不典型，但可能混合状态。

00:17:47.712 --> 00:17:58.632
Neurological findings can include confusion, focal-like deficits, seizures or coma. The older name nonketotic coma does not mean coma is mandatory.
神经表现可包括混乱、局灶样缺损、抽搐或昏迷；旧称“非酮性昏迷”并不表示必须昏迷。

00:17:58.632 --> 00:18:11.544
Assess infection, stroke, cardiac disease and other triggers as well as glucose. Do not let an HHS label dismiss a new focal deficit or postpone urgent definitive evaluation.
除糖外还需评感染、中风、心病等触发；不能因HHS标签忽视新局灶缺损或推迟紧急确定评估。

00:18:11.544 --> 00:18:24.192
DKA and HHS share hyperglycemic stress, fluid loss and electrolyte risk. The relative ketone and osmotic components differ, and a patient can have features of both.
DKA与HHS都可有高糖应激、丢液及电解质风险；酮及渗透成分比例不同，一个人也可能两者都有。

00:18:24.192 --> 00:18:36.480
Typical age and diabetes type can guide suspicion but cannot serve as strict gates. A new presentation may not come with a prior diagnosis or a familiar medication list.
典型年龄和分型可引导怀疑，却不能作严格门槛；首次呈现可能没有旧诊断或熟悉药单。

00:18:36.480 --> 00:18:49.344
Neither an isolated high glucose nor the absence of fruity breath supplies the full diagnosis. Laboratory evaluation of ketones, acid-base balance and osmolality may be needed.
单个高糖或无水果味都不能提供完整诊断，可能需要酮、酸碱及渗透压化验。

00:18:49.344 --> 00:19:02.520
Communicate suspected hyperglycemic crisis and the observed consequences without inventing a definitive subtype. Timely support and destination planning do not require perfect classification.
应传达疑高糖危象及观察后果，而不自创确定亚型；及时支持和目的地计划不需要完美分型。

00:19:02.520 --> 00:19:16.728
The selected modern adult consensus requires ketosis and metabolic acidosis alongside diabetes or hyperglycemia. It no longer makes the older Nancy value above eighteen a universal DKA gate.
选读现代成人共识要求糖尿病或高糖，同时有酮及代谢酸中毒，不再把旧Nancy高于18当通用DKA门槛。

00:19:16.728 --> 00:19:30.360
DKA can occur without marked hyperglycemia, including with SGLT two medicines, reduced intake or pregnancy. A not-very-high glucose must not overrule a concerning illness pattern.
DKA可无明显高糖，例如SGLT2药、摄入少或妊娠背景，因此糖不很高不能推翻危险急病模式。

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:42.552
Most field assessments cannot establish every laboratory criterion. State the suspicion and what is actually measured rather than declaring normal glucose means no metabolic emergency.
多数现场不能确定全部化验标准；应说怀疑及真正实测，不能称糖正常就没有代谢急症。

00:19:42.552 --> 00:19:54.216
International hospital insulin and glucose-fluid algorithms are not new PCP orders. Use the current local pathway, clinical consultation and urgent definitive assessment.
国际医院胰岛素及含糖液算法，不是新PCP医嘱；需用现行当地路径、临床咨询及紧急确定评估。

00:19:54.216 --> 00:20:05.568
A fifty-six-year-old with type-two diabetes takes empagliflozin. During an illness with little intake and repeated vomiting, breathing becomes deep at twenty-eight per minute.
一位56岁二型糖尿病者用恩格列净，急病摄入少并反复吐，呼吸转深、每分钟28次。

00:20:05.568 --> 00:20:17.400
Glucose is nine point eight. That is below older dramatic DKA values, but it does not explain away a possible euglycemic ketotic crisis or another serious cause.
糖9.8低于旧书典型极高值，但不能消除可能正常或不显高糖的酮性危象，或其他重因。

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:30.480
Assess airway, perfusion, glucose reliability and the illness timeline, and consider other causes of deep breathing such as sepsis. Do not assume that the drug history alone confirms DKA.
需查气道、灌注、糖可靠性及病程，并考虑脓毒症等深呼吸原因；药史本身不能确诊DKA。

00:20:30.480 --> 00:20:43.200
Arrange urgent evaluation, indicated support and a clear alert about the medicine, reduced intake, vomiting and breathing pattern. Do not attempt to normalize the number with extra insulin.
应紧急评估、有指征支持，清楚预警药物、摄入少、呕吐及呼吸模式；不能试用额外胰岛素把数字调正常。

00:20:43.200 --> 00:20:53.280
Support current airway and respiratory needs and prepare for vomiting. Preserve necessary compensatory ventilation while watching for fatigue or failure.
需支持当前气道呼吸并备呕吐，在警惕疲劳失败时保留必要代偿通气。

00:20:53.280 --> 00:21:05.328
Assess actual depletion, perfusion and congestion before an indicated fluid plan. Cardiac or kidney disease, pregnancy and age can change the risk and response.
有指征液体计划前需评真实不足、灌注及淤血；心肾病、妊娠及年龄可改变风险反应。

00:21:05.328 --> 00:21:18.360
Monitor useful rhythm, glucose and functional trends. Do not automatically give insulin, bicarbonate or potassium, and do not delay urgent conveyance for an arbitrary volume target.
需监有用节律、糖及功能趋势；不能自动给胰岛素、碳酸氢钠或钾，也不能为任意量目标延误紧急转运。

00:21:18.360 --> 00:21:31.440
Seek the precipitant, including infection, missed delivery or another acute event, and communicate it. Treat access and device problems compassionately rather than labelling the person noncompliant.
应寻找感染、药输送中断等触发或其他急事件并传达；要有同情心处理获取和器械问题，不能只贴不依从标签。

00:21:31.440 --> 00:21:41.808
Cortisol supports metabolic responses to stress and normal vascular responsiveness. Deficiency can make an acute illness much harder to tolerate.
皮质醇支持应激代谢及正常血管反应，缺乏会使急病更难耐受。

00:21:41.808 --> 00:21:52.128
Aldosterone promotes sodium retention and potassium excretion in the kidney. Primary adrenal failure can reduce both cortisol and mineralocorticoid function.
醛固酮在肾促保钠及排钾，原发肾上腺失败可同时降低皮质醇及盐皮质功能。

00:21:52.128 --> 00:22:05.688
Pituitary failure or glucocorticoid suppression can reduce cortisol while aldosterone remains relatively preserved. Therefore not every adrenal-crisis patient has high potassium or the same skin findings.
垂体失败或糖皮质抑制可减少皮质醇，而醛固酮相对保留，因此并非所有危象都高钾或同样皮肤表现。

00:22:05.688 --> 00:22:19.176
Vomiting, weakness, hypotension, low glucose or confusion in a compatible history should raise concern. Do not wait for a laboratory cortisol or a classic pigmentation change to seek help.
相符病史下的吐、无力、低压、低糖或混乱，应引担忧；不能等皮质醇化验或典型色素变才求援。

00:22:19.176 --> 00:22:32.520
Ask about Addison disease, pituitary insufficiency, prior crises and a prescribed emergency hydrocortisone kit. The patient may carry a steroid alert card or individualized plan.
需问Addison病、垂体不足、既往危象及处方紧急氢化可的松套件，患者可能带类固醇警示卡或个体计划。

00:22:32.520 --> 00:22:45.456
The current local guideline uses three weeks or more of glucocorticoid treatment as a risk-history marker. Actual suppression depends on exposure and the individual; it is not a perfect bedside test.
当前当地指导把至少三周糖皮质治疗列为风险史线索；真实抑制依暴露及个人而异，不是完美床边测试。

00:22:45.456 --> 00:22:56.352
Illness, trauma or vomiting can raise need or prevent retention of the usual replacement. Ask what was taken, kept down or injected before arrival.
疾病、创伤或呕吐可增需要，或使平常替代无法保留；需问到达前吃了什么、留住什么或注射了什么。

00:22:56.352 --> 00:23:09.264
Do not advise abrupt cessation from a chronic steroid history. Excess exposure can produce Cushing features while the normal stress axis is suppressed, so appearance alone does not settle reserve.
不能因慢性类固醇史就建议骤停；过量暴露可有Cushing表现，同时正常应激轴受抑，因此外观不能确定储备。

00:23:09.264 --> 00:23:20.664
Current E zero two combines compatible signs such as vomiting, weakness, hypotension, low glucose or confusion with a qualifying adrenal or steroid history.
当前E02把呕吐、无力、低压、低糖或混乱等相符表现，与合资格肾上腺或类固醇史结合。

00:23:20.664 --> 00:23:31.656
The published pathway also requires an existing hydrocortisone prescription for adrenal insufficiency. It is not a blanket steroid order for any undifferentiated shock.
公开路径还要求已有用于肾上腺不足的氢化可的松处方，因此不是所有未分化休克的普遍类固醇医嘱。

00:23:31.656 --> 00:23:47.064
Request the required consultation early and report previous doses. The guideline addresses treatment even after prior patient administration, so obtain an explicit plan rather than ignoring or automatically duplicating that dose.
应及早请求所需咨询并报告先前剂量；指导涉及患者先自行给后仍需处理，因此需取得明确计划，不能忽略或自动重复。

00:23:47.064 --> 00:23:57.000
Continue ABC support and correction of associated low glucose or hypoperfusion. Do not walk a suspected crisis patient to the ambulance.
需继续ABC支持，纠相关低糖或低灌注；不能让疑危象者走去救护车。

00:23:57.000 --> 00:24:08.544
The checked adult PCP monograph specifies one hundred milligrams of hydrocortisone directly over one minute, with prior CliniCall consultation for acute adrenal crisis.
核对成人PCP专论规定急性肾上腺危象氢化可的松100毫克直接给入历时一分钟，且需先CliniCall咨询。

00:24:08.544 --> 00:24:22.224
IV is preferred, but IM is acceptable early if vascular access is delayed or unobtainable. Do not keep attempting a difficult vein while the authorized alternative is being unnecessarily delayed.
静脉优先，但通路延迟或不可得时可早肌注；不能反复尝试困难静脉而不必要拖延已获准替代。

00:24:22.224 --> 00:24:34.920
Use the actual product instructions, trained preparation, indication and contraindication checks. A one-hundred-milligram vial label does not by itself tell you the final reconstituted volume.
需用真实产品说明、受训准备、指征及禁忌核查；100毫克瓶标本身不能说明复溶后最终体积。

00:24:34.920 --> 00:24:50.448
EMR assistance is limited to collecting the patient own medicine in E zero two, not preparing or injecting it. Adult PCP authorization does not establish a pediatric dose or a steroid order for all asthma or sepsis.
E02中EMR协助只限收取患者自有药，不可准备注射；成人PCP授权不建立儿童剂量，也非所有哮喘脓毒症的类固醇医嘱。

00:24:50.448 --> 00:25:01.080
A thirty-eight-year-old with Addison disease and a prescribed rescue kit has repeated vomiting during an illness. It is unclear how much usual replacement was retained.
一位38岁Addison病且有处方救援套件者，急病反复吐，平常替代药留住多少不清。

00:25:01.080 --> 00:25:12.120
There is weakness and confusion, pressure eighty-two over fifty and glucose three point two. This needs immediate support and safe correction of the low glucose.
患者无力混乱，血压82/50、糖3.2，需要立即支持并安全纠低糖。

00:25:12.120 --> 00:25:23.568
Obtain the actual medicine and prior-dose history, request the mandatory consultation and use the eligible hydrocortisone pathway with appropriate training and product checks.
需取得真实药及先前剂量史，进行强制咨询，并在适当训练产品核查下使用合资格氢化可的松路径。

00:25:23.568 --> 00:25:35.784
Do not walk the patient or promise immediate normalization after injection. Reassess perfusion, breathing, glucose and possible infection while arranging urgent conveyance.
不能步行搬运，也不能承诺注射后立刻正常；需在紧急转运中复评灌注、呼吸、糖及可能感染。

00:25:35.784 --> 00:25:48.360
Thyroid hormone influences metabolism, temperature regulation, cardiac function and responsiveness. The hypothalamus-pituitary-thyroid axis helps regulate its production.
甲状腺激素影响代谢、温度调节、心功能及反应，下丘脑垂体甲状腺轴帮助调产。

00:25:48.360 --> 00:26:01.536
Low function can cause fatigue, cold intolerance, slowed thinking and constipation. Excess function can cause heat intolerance, tremor, rapid pulse and increased metabolic demand.
功能低可疲倦、怕冷、思考慢及便秘；过强可怕热、颤抖、脉快及代谢需求增加。

00:26:01.536 --> 00:26:11.376
These chronic patterns do not diagnose an emergency on their own. Ask about current change, medicine delivery, infection and actual organ function.
这些慢性模式本身不能诊断急症，需问当前改变、药物送达、感染及真实器官功能。

00:26:11.376 --> 00:26:26.832
Thyrotoxicosis means excess thyroid-hormone effect and need not always mean increased gland synthesis. Severe decompensation requires urgent support and definitive care, not an improvised field thyroid regimen.
甲状腺毒症指激素效应过强，不一定都为腺合成增多；严重失代偿需紧急支持确定照护，不是现场自创甲状腺配方。

00:26:26.832 --> 00:26:38.136
Thyroid storm can occur when thyrotoxicosis decompensates during infection, another stressor or treatment interruption. No single temperature or pulse establishes it.
甲状腺毒症在感染、其他应激或治疗中断时可失代偿为危象；单个温度或脉率不能确诊。

00:26:38.136 --> 00:26:50.736
Look for the overall severe pattern: marked heat, rapid or irregular rhythm, gastrointestinal symptoms and altered mental status, sometimes with heart failure or shock.
需看整体重模式：明显高热、快速或不规则节律、胃肠症状及精神变化，有时心衰或休克。

00:26:50.736 --> 00:27:03.984
Sepsis, toxic exposure and other causes can overlap. Assess glucose, breathing, perfusion, temperature and the medication/history timeline while obtaining urgent clinical help.
脓毒症、中毒等可重叠；求紧急临床援助时，应查糖、呼吸、灌注、温度及药史时间线。

00:27:03.984 --> 00:27:16.104
Provide indicated temperature and ABC support through the actual pathway. Specialist antithyroid, beta-blocking and other treatments are not a generic independent PCP bundle.
需依真实路径提供有指征温度及ABC支持；专科抗甲状腺、β阻断等治疗，并非通用PCP独立套餐。

00:27:16.104 --> 00:27:29.472
Severe hypothyroid decompensation is often called myxedema coma, although the patient need not be fully comatose. Infection, cold, medicines or another stressor can precipitate it.
严重甲低失代偿常称黏液性水肿昏迷，但不必已完全昏迷；感染、冷、药或其他应激可触发。

00:27:29.472 --> 00:27:42.720
Reduced responsiveness, hypoventilation, cold temperature, bradycardia and hypotension can occur. Check glucose and consider electrolyte disturbance without diagnosing from one sign.
可能反应下降、低通气、低体温、心动过缓及低压；需测糖并考虑电解质问题，不能靠一个征确诊。

00:27:42.720 --> 00:27:54.192
Support effective ventilation and oxygenation, use careful temperature management and treat confirmed low glucose through the current route. Escalate urgently for deterioration.
应支持有效通气氧合、谨慎温度管理，并经当前途径纠确认低糖；恶化时要紧急升级。

00:27:54.192 --> 00:28:07.032
Do not give a textbook dopamine, thyroid-hormone or large dextrose recipe independently, and do not use age, sex or absent fever to exclude another serious infection or endocrine cause.
不能独立照教材给多巴胺、甲状腺激素或大糖配方，也不能以年龄、性别或无热排除其他严重感染或内分泌因。

00:28:07.032 --> 00:28:32.400
In this original case, a patient with known hypothyroidism has been ill and is now drowsy, cold and breathing shallowly. Recognize the breathing and perfusion threats before trying to name the endocrine diagnosis. Assess airway and effective ventilation, measure glucose and temperature, and obtain medication and baseline history while your partner arranges urgent assistance.
原创病例中，既往甲低患者近期患病，现嗜睡、发冷且呼吸浅。确定内分泌诊断前，应先识别呼吸及灌注威胁。需评气道及有效通气、实测血糖体温，并在伙伴安排紧急协助时取得用药及基线史。

00:28:32.400 --> 00:29:01.392
Severe hypothyroid decompensation is possible, but infection, environmental exposure, medicines or more than one problem may coexist. A lack of fever is not infection clearance. Provide indicated breathing, glucose, temperature and perfusion support through current pathways, reassess the response and pre-alert with the observed findings. Do not independently copy a hormone, vasopressor or fixed fluid recipe.
可能是严重甲低失代偿，但感染、环境暴露、药物或多个问题可以共存。无发热不等于排除感染。应经现行路径给予有指征的呼吸、血糖、温度及灌注支持，复评反应并用实际发现预警；不能独立照搬激素、升压药或固定输液配方。

00:29:01.392 --> 00:29:11.712
ADH, or vasopressin, primarily increases water reabsorption through its renal effect. This is distinct from aldosterone-mediated sodium handling.
ADH即血管加压素，其肾作用主要增水重吸收，不同于醛固酮介导钠处理。

00:29:11.712 --> 00:29:23.808
Deficient ADH effect can cause large dilute urine losses, as in diabetes insipidus. This is a water-balance disorder, not the same as diabetes mellitus or glucose in urine.
ADH效应不足可如尿崩症般大量稀尿，这是水平衡问题，不等于糖尿病或尿糖。

00:29:23.808 --> 00:29:36.216
Excess ADH effect can retain water and contribute to dilutional low sodium. Neurological symptoms require assessment and proper chemistry rather than guessing sodium from appearance.
ADH效应过多可潴水并造成稀释低钠；神经症状需评估及正确化验，不能凭外观猜钠。

00:29:36.216 --> 00:29:50.544
Ask about intake/output, pituitary or brain disease, medicines and the timeline. Do not automatically give plain water, salt, fluid restriction or hormone replacement from a suspected label.
需问出入量、垂体脑病、药及时间线，不能从疑似标签自动给清水、盐、限液或激素替代。

00:29:50.544 --> 00:30:02.400
Parathyroid hormone helps raise available calcium through kidney and bone effects and the vitamin-D pathway. Calcium regulation is not simply a two-hormone on-off switch.
甲状旁腺激素通过肾、骨及维生素D路径帮助升可用钙，钙调节并非简单两激素开关。

00:30:02.400 --> 00:30:12.960
Calcitonin is thyroid-derived and has a different role. Keep the thyroid metabolic-hormone pathway separate from parathyroid and calcium physiology.
降钙素来自甲状腺但作用不同，应把甲状腺代谢激素路径与甲旁及钙生理分开。

00:30:12.960 --> 00:30:25.872
Calcium disturbance can affect neuromuscular and cardiac function, with possible tingling, spasm, weakness or ECG change. None supplies a precise blood concentration.
钙异常可影响神经肌肉及心功能，可能麻、痉挛、无力或心电变，但都不能提供精确血浓度。

00:30:25.872 --> 00:30:38.256
Use the clinical history, actual laboratory information and appropriate support. A physiology reading does not authorize empiric calcium for every symptom or a single ECG interval.
需用病史、真实化验及适当支持；生理阅读不授权对每个症状或单个心电间期经验性给钙。

00:30:38.256 --> 00:30:50.736
Ask what medicine was actually delivered and when, including a pump interruption, injection issue or vomiting after tablets. A prescribed plan and delivered treatment are different facts.
需问真实送达何药何时，包括泵中断、注射问题或片后吐；处方计划与实际送达是不同事实。

00:30:50.736 --> 00:31:01.200
Compare that with food, activity, infection symptoms, pregnancy and other stress. The balance can change even when the patient followed the usual prescription.
应与食物、活动、感染症状、妊娠及应激比较；即使照平常处方，平衡也可能改变。

00:31:01.200 --> 00:31:12.000
Kidney or liver dysfunction can modify medicine handling, glycogen availability and fluid risk. Ask about the baseline and verified recent findings.
肾肝功能异常可改药处理、糖原可用量及液体风险；需问基线和已核近期发现。

00:31:12.000 --> 00:31:25.992
Explore practical access barriers without blame and use the patient preferred communication support. Do not change an insulin pump program or long-term regimen without actual authority and an agreed clinical plan.
应不责备地探索实际获取障碍，采用患者偏好沟通支持；没有真实权限及商定临床计划，不能改泵程序或长期方案。

00:31:25.992 --> 00:31:37.632
After correction of low glucose, ask whether the actual problem resolved. A patient can have a normal value and still have a stroke, infection, injury or toxic effect.
纠低糖后需问真实问题是否解决；即使糖正常，仍可能有中风、感染、伤或毒性效应。

00:31:37.632 --> 00:31:51.480
In a suspected high-glucose crisis, follow breathing, perfusion and rhythm with the illness course. A lower glucose alone does not prove resolution of ketosis, acidosis or hyperosmolality.
疑高糖危象时，应随病程追呼吸、灌注及节律；糖降本身不证明酮、酸中毒或高渗已解决。

00:31:51.480 --> 00:32:03.408
In adrenal crisis, accurate eligibility, dose history and early consultation matter alongside ABC support. Do not assume that a hormone injection instantly reverses shock.
肾上腺危象中，准确资格、剂量史及早咨询，与ABC支持同样重要；不能认为打一针激素立即逆休克。

00:32:03.408 --> 00:32:14.880
If the response does not fit, reconsider delivery, timing, recurrence and another cause. Explain that revision clearly to the team and receiving clinicians.
反应不符时需重想送达、时刻、复发及其他原因，并向团队接收人员清楚说明修订。

00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:24.768
Begin with the current patient, not only a glucose number. State awareness, breathing, circulation and the reason the case needs urgent evaluation.
应先说当前患者，而不只一个糖值；要有意识、呼吸、循环及需紧急评估原因。

00:32:24.768 --> 00:32:37.512
Give measured glucose with units and times, relevant medicines or established hormone disease and the illness timeline. Preserve last known well when neurological disease remains possible.
应给带单位时刻实测糖、相关药或已知激素病，以及病程；仍可能神经病时保留最后正常。

00:32:37.512 --> 00:32:50.304
Report the actual product, amount, concentration, route and time, including earlier rescue doses and the required consultation. Then describe both the number and functional response.
要报真实产品、量、浓度、途径时刻，含先前救援剂及所需咨询，再描述数值和功能反应。

00:32:50.304 --> 00:33:02.904
Mention recurrence, persistent focal findings, possible euglycemic crisis or unresolved shock. Accurate uncertainty helps the receiving team prepare the right investigation and care.
需提复发、持续局灶、可能不显高糖危象或未解决休克；准确不确定，有助接收方准备正确检查照护。

00:33:02.904 --> 00:33:13.776
For low glucose, explain the route from command following, swallowing and IV availability, then calculate the actual product volume and predict the response.
低糖时，应从遵指令、吞咽及静脉可得解释途径，再算真实产品体积并预测反应。

00:33:13.776 --> 00:33:25.800
For suspected DKA or HHS, explain two mechanisms and why one glucose does not describe the complete problem. Include ventilation and potassium risk.
疑DKA或HHS时，应解释两种机制，以及单糖为何不能描述全问题，并包括通气及钾风险。

00:33:25.800 --> 00:33:39.000
For adrenal crisis, state the compatible illness, qualifying history, prescription and mandatory consultation. Include the adult regimen and what you do if IV access is delayed.
肾上腺危象时，应说相符急病、合资格史、处方及强制咨询，含成人方案及静脉延迟怎么办。

00:33:39.000 --> 00:33:49.728
Finish each answer with an alternative diagnosis and a reassessment that could change your plan. Naming a hormone or a medicine is only the beginning of the explanation.
每个答案最后加替代诊断及会改计划的复评；报出激素或药名只是解释起点。

00:33:49.728 --> 00:33:59.472
You should now explain the major endocrine feedback and glucose-regulation roles without using age, body size or an insulin label as a diagnostic shortcut.
现在应能解释主要内分泌反馈及糖调节，不把年龄体型或胰岛素标签当诊断捷径。

00:33:59.472 --> 00:34:09.216
You should choose an airway-safe low-glucose route, calculate D ten correctly, distinguish the current nasal glucagon product and investigate recurrence.
应能选气道安全纠低糖途径、正确算D10、区分当前鼻用胰高血糖素，并调查复发。

00:34:09.216 --> 00:34:20.880
You should connect DKA and HHS mechanisms to breathing, fluid and potassium risk, and recognize adrenal or thyroid decompensation with actual local treatment boundaries.
应能把DKA、HHS机制连到呼吸、液体和钾风险，并在真实当地边界内识别肾上腺或甲状腺失代偿。

00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:30.792
Complete the bilingual reading and original practice, then use the integrated school cases to rehearse a changing-patient assessment and accurate handover.
完成中英阅读及原创练习，再用学校要求的综合情境排练动态患者评估和准确交接。
